{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fbcb503748b8a648fa7653255de617357455010744261ff1664040b061efd202","digest":{"component_or_area":"inbound_probe / backend adapter abstraction","key_entities":["inbound_probe.py","adapters/jira/probe.py","adapters/jira/backend.py","run_differs.py","_backend.py","SupportsAbsenceProbe","ProbeBranch","ProbeResult","probe_remote","reconcile_helpers.route_inbound_probe","JIRA_URL","JIRA_USER","JIRA_API_TOKEN","RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES"],"problem_keywords":["vendor-specific probe","backend neutrality","capability pattern","jira probe","code relocation"],"propositions":["Jira-specific probe logic (URL construction, basic-auth GET, status-name classification) is embedded in core inbound_probe.py, blocking other backends from implementing their own probe variants","The probe dispatch in run_differs.py:369 calls the probe module directly without a capability abstraction, preventing a second backend from dropping in","The neutral probe vocabulary (ProbeBranch, ProbeResult, ProbeConfigError) must remain at package root per ADR 0035, separate from vendor mechanics","The SupportsAbsenceProbe capability protocol routes the probe through the backend at runtime, allowing each backend to implement probe_remote differently while degrading to UNREACHABLE if unsupported"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787587161148529001,"uuid":"07b4a7a5-91c3-44ca-83ad-457e14856c0f"}